        { "host": "B", "text": "Before anyone panics, the limits are substantial. The key was never factored. SecurityWeek says that would take an estimated 500,000 to 1 million core-years. The attack needs roughly 4 billion signing queries made in advance, and it doesn't recover the private key. Two of the bigger-sounding figures, a 1,600 times improvement and a 30 times cheaper batch method, are theoretical estimates, and the batch method has not been implemented." },
