        { "host": "A", "text": "A paper from Google DeepMind and Google Quantum AI researchers put language model agents to work writing quantum programs inside the Lean theorem prover, so every program the agents produce is machine-checked for correctness and for cost." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "And they improved on what people had already built?" },
        { "host": "A", "text": "On arXiv they report gains over prior baselines of up to 1.4x on parallel search, 290x on quantum arithmetic, and on simulations relevant to fusion, photochemistry and drug metabolism, 11x, 8x and 2.5x." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "The formal verification is what makes this unusual. Most agent results you have to take on trust. These ones are proof-checked." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "Though this is a preprint, so it is not peer reviewed, and arXiv is the only source for it. The arXiv page shows no affiliations, there's no accompanying DeepMind blog post, and the speedups are measured against baselines the authors chose themselves." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "transition",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "A", "text": "Now to security, which took up most of this weekend." }
      ]
